# Interface Vision (Synthwave / Retrowave Theme)

Sidequest Mail should feel like a neon-soaked night drive — but work like Proton Mail.
The chrome and gradients are the skin, not the mechanics.
Everything below is aesthetic and optional; the core email flow (read, reply, file, delete) must always be instant.

---

## Layout Grid

| Screen       | Synthwave Concept        | Behavior                                                                 |
|:-------------|:-------------------------|:-------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **Inbox**    | The Neon Grid            | Emails sit on the perspective grid. Unread emails pulse with magenta light. |
|              |                          | Opening one "locks on" — the grid lines stabilize.                       |
| **Folders**  | The Archives             | Each folder is a data crate. Navigating there shows: *"Archive Accessed."* |
| **Sent**     | The Transmission         | You sent the signal. "Signal Lost" (in a good way) energy.               |
| **Trash**    | The Void                 | Where data gets erased from the grid. Dragging an email there dissolves it. |
|              |                          | Restoring it is "rewinding the tape."                                    |
| **Drafts**   | The Studio               | Still being mixed. Waveforms scattered, half-formed beats.               |

---

## Navigation Grid

| Key          | Action                   | Flavor Text                              |
|:-------------|:-------------------------|:-----------------------------------------|
| **Arrow Keys** | Move focus between emails | VHS static chirp sound                 |
| **Spacebar**   | Open selected email      | *"Loading track..."*                     |
| **Enter**      | Reply while reading      | *"Sending signal."*                      |
| **Drag & Drop** | Move between folders     | Data cassette swap animation             |

